AB  - We release NovEdit, 1.2 million edit events from 3,400 consenting novice programmers across four terms, with two benchmark tasks: predicting the next action class (edit, run, delete block, seek help, idle) and predicting whether a student will recover from an error within five minutes. Sequence models outperform count-based baselines on next action (macro-F1 0.58 vs 0.47) but not on recovery (AUC 0.71 vs 0.70). We document collection, consent and splits grouped by student and term.
