AB  - We audited the documentation of 37 publicly released learning-interaction datasets against an adapted datasheet. Fewer than a third reported how consent was obtained (30%) and fewer than a fifth stated how train and test splits were formed (19%). Only 4 reported the share of students who opted out. We propose a 12-question supplement for learning traces covering consent, granularity, de-identification, split units and known artifacts of the collection platform.
