TY  - JOUR
TI  - Group-Aware Splits for Educational Sequence Data: How Student Overlap Inflates Reported Accuracy
AU  - Ferreira, Ana
AU  - Kowalczyk, Piotr
T2  - Journal of Educational Data Mining
VL  - 15
IS  - 2
SP  - 44
EP  - 67
PY  - 2023
DA  - 2026/07/24/
AB  - Educational datasets are made of many short sequences from relatively few students. When windows or attempts are split into train and test sets at random, the same student appears on both sides and models can learn the student rather than the behavior. We re-ran the evaluations of eleven prediction tasks on five public-style datasets with random splits and with splits grouped by student. Grouped splits lowered reported performance by 4 to 17 points of AUC or F1, with the largest drops for tasks built from short windows. We give a checklist for detecting and reporting this leakage.
LA  - en
KW  - data leakage
KW  - cross-validation
KW  - evaluation
KW  - sequence data
