N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><h1>IDETrace leakage - found 07-24</h1><p><span class="citation" data-citation="%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2Flocal%2FmyLibrary%2Fitems%2FGSEDVCQM%22%5D%7D%5D%7D">(<span class="citation-item">Ferreira and Kowalczyk, 2023</span>)</span> this paper describes exactly what happened: windows from the same student in train and test. random split over windows, sklearn default. ugh</p><ul><li>their off-task drop was 17 pts, struggle 14. ours: macro-F1 0.81 -&gt; 0.74 with GroupKFold on student_id. in line with them</li><li>do the student-id probe they suggest and report it (my quick run: way above chance, ~0.5 top-1 over 160 students)</li><li>rebuttal: report BOTH numbers, say we found it ourselves, cite this + Kaufman 2012</li><li>fix split script: group by student id, then also hold out a lab section as a sanity check</li></ul></div>
