AB  - Behavior classifiers in learning analytics are usually summarized by macro-F1. We show on three datasets that models with similar macro-F1 can differ widely in calibration on minority states, which matters when predictions trigger interventions. We recommend reporting per-class F1, expected calibration error per class, and a reliability diagram for the state that will drive an intervention.
